<h3 class="faq-item__q">What lighting is recommended for data centers?</h3>
<p class="faq-item__a">Data centers require highly efficient, low-heat LED lighting with precise optical control to illuminate server aisles without wasting energy. Continuous linear runs or strategically placed low-bays are ideal.</p>
</article>
<article class="faq-item">
<h3 class="faq-item__q">What controls do data center facilities need?</h3>
<p class="faq-item__a">Data centers rely heavily on aisle-level occupancy sensors. Since server aisles are infrequently occupied, fixtures should remain off or dimmed to 10% until a technician enters the aisle.</p>
</article>
